# JS systems

## Style

- ESM (`"type": "module"`). Plain JS with JSDoc `@param` / `@type` — no TypeScript.
- File header stating what the module owns and any load-bearing order.
- Import Babylon from deep paths (`@babylonjs/core/...`), not the barrel.
- Classes own construction + `update(dt, …)` + optional `async warmUp()` / `setVisible`.

## Settings

- Tunables on flat `S` in `core/settings.js`. Overlay widgets from `SCHEMA` (`t: "f"|"b"|"e"`).
- `onChange(key, fn)` only when rebuild is needed; otherwise sample `S` next frame.
- Writes via `set(k, v)` — never from the render loop.

## GPU / materials

- `ShaderLanguage.WGSL` on every `ShaderMaterial` / `ProceduralTexture`.
- Shader names must match `shaders/registry.js` (`prop`, `snow`, `staticDepth`, …).
- Prefer `bindMatrixArray` over `setMatrices` for cascade uploads (avoids GC).
- Opaque casters: `ShadowSystem.registerCaster` with the real depth vertex program; also `DepthPass.registerCaster` for post.

## Frame wiring (`main.js`)

Order is intentional — preserve or update comments when changing it:

```
pollInput → character.update → pedestal/giant collision → contact
→ camera → post/sky/shadows → pedestals → giant → (didHit → applyHit/playHit)
→ avatar → bow → arrows → terrain → spray → render → endFrame
```

Input edges (`jumpPressed`, `emotePressed`, `drawPressed`, `openPressed`) clear in `endFrame()`.

## Combat notes

- Bow grips LeftHand (skeleton refresh required); arrows are a 10-slot FIFO pool (flight + stuck).
- Giant melee hits only on contact window + SFX; arrow hits call `giant.playHit(zone)`.
